# DOS batch files ship to real MS-DOS and MUST have CRLF line terminators.
#
# COMMAND.COM does not reliably parse an LF-only .BAT: on the fleet's Win98
# box an LF-only file gave "Bad command or file name" and, with `@echo off`
# as its first line, printed "OFF" and stopped. These files had been LF in
# git the whole time and worked on the fleet only because somebody had once
# published them from a Windows machine, which converted them by accident -
# so the copies on the share were 57 bytes larger than the copies in git and
# nothing recorded why. Publishing straight from a Linux dev host (which is
# what retro_upload does, byte for byte) would have pushed the LF versions
# onto every DOS box and broken PLAY, NETUP and the MS-DOS mode startup file
# in one go.
*.BAT   text eol=crlf
*.TPL   text eol=crlf
CONFIG.SYS.dosbox text eol=crlf
